      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like you're carrying something heavy, and that stillness can feel isolating. Those moments of disconnect, even with your own hands, are a sign your mind is asking for a gentler kind of attention. You're not \"taking up space\" — you're pausing in a world that doesn't stop, and that counts for something. If the quiet feels too loud, maybe start with one small, tangible comfort—a warm drink, a soft blanket, or just naming one thing you can touch. You don't have to fix everything today, just breathe through this minute.",
